        what: "No shared utility drives a canvas/WebGL animation with a SYNTHETIC, non-realtime clock for frame-accurate capture. render/gifRecorder.js (vendored gifenc, MIT) encodes an array of already-captured RGBA frames but has no opinion on how they were collected; its one caller, blob-selfie.html, hand-rolls its own loop (a direct theta sweep with a setTimeout(r, 0) yield). ui/canvasRecorder.js and render/blobRecorder.js both capture via canvas.captureStream() + MediaRecorder -- REAL-TIME, wall-clock-driven, and already measured (okf/claims/the-mp4-that-is-not-an-mp4.md) to be paint-driven rather than clock-driven.",
        how: "Read roboshoes/canvas-recorder (MIT, github.com/roboshoes/canvas-recorder) end to end -- not to port its file, which pulls in jszip/lodash/commander/file-saver this codebase has no other use for and whose CLI half (ffmpeg PNG-sequence merge) duplicates ai-bridge/ffmpegStatic.js, already vendored here. The one idea worth taking is the pattern: a draw(context, time) loop where `time` is a SYNTHETIC accumulator (1000/fps per captured frame) rather than performance.now(), so the OUTPUT is evenly paced regardless of how long each frame actually took to render or encode -- a scene too slow for live 60fps can still produce a smooth 60fps capture. That is a small, self-contained module (well under the size of gifRecorder.js), not a dependency.",
        why: "This is not a missing feature nobody asked for -- it is a gap in something this engine already leans on twice (GIF export, real-time video export) and re-solves ad hoc each time. And it is a natural fit for a codebase built around reproducibility: a synthetic per-frame clock means the SAME animation captured twice produces IDENTICAL frames, the same property this tree already insists on for its seeded RNGs and ?seed=N repro URLs (world/vendoredLicences.mjs-adjacent culture, not GPU determinism -- this is JS-side timing, no device involved). Pairing it with the EXISTING encodeGif() and ffmpegStatic.js would give any future canvas/WebGL page frame-accurate GIF or MP4 capture without a bespoke loop, rather than blob-selfie.html's approach being copied forward by hand each time.",
